  "result": "Perfect! All 52 tests pass. I've added two new functions to `src/invoices.js`:\n\n**addLine(invoice, { sku, qty })** \u2014 Adds a line to a draft invoice, or increases qty if the SKU already exists. Validates qty and SKU the same way as createInvoice. Returns NOT_DRAFT if the invoice isn't in draft status.\n\n**removeLine(invoice, sku)** \u2014 Removes a line from a draft invoice. Returns:\n- NOT_DRAFT if the invoice isn't draft\n- LINE_NOT_FOUND if the SKU isn't on the invoice\n- NO_LINES if removing it would leave the invoice empty\n\nBoth functions preserve immutability (never mutate the input invoice or its lines array).\n\nThe tests cover:\n- Adding new lines and increasing quantities\n- NOT_DRAFT checks for both functions\n- All validation errors (QTY_INVALID, UNKNOWN_SKU, LINE_NOT_FOUND, NO_LINES)\n- Immutability\n- Chaining operations together\n- Accumulating quantities across multiple addLine calls\n\nReady for the next request.",
